---
import Doc from '../../../layouts/Doc.astro';
import Pager from '../../../components/Pager.astro';
const slug = 'getting-started/quick-start';
---
<Doc slug={slug} title="Quick start">
  <h1>Quick start</h1>
  <p class="lede">Configure a model and run cortex in under a minute.</p>

  <h2>The fastest possible start</h2>
  <p>cortex needs one thing before it can start: a model. Two environment variables are enough:</p>
  <pre><code>export LLM_MODEL=gpt-4o
export LLM_API_KEY=sk-...
cortex</code></pre>

  <h2>Interactive mode</h2>
  <p>Run cortex with no arguments to start an interactive session in your current directory:</p>
  <pre><code>cortex                                   # interactive
cortex --prompt "summarize the TODOs"    # one turn, then exit
cortex --config reviewer.yaml            # a specific config, no cascade
cortex --version</code></pre>

  <h2>Non-interactive mode</h2>
  <p>
    <code>--prompt</code> writes the assistant's answer to <strong>stdout</strong> and
    everything else — tool activity, notices, errors — to <strong>stderr</strong>, so it composes:
  </p>
  <pre><code>cortex --prompt "list every exported function in internal/ui" > api.txt</code></pre>
  <p>See <a href="/docs/guides/non-interactive/">Non-interactive mode</a> for the full picture.</p>

  <h2>A config file for repeat use</h2>
  <p>If you don't want to pass env vars every time, write a config file:</p>
  <pre><code># ~/.config/cortex/config.yaml
model:
  provider: openrouter
  name: deepseek/deepseek-v3.2
  api_key: $OPENROUTER_API_KEY</code></pre>
  <p>
    The <code>$</code> prefix reads the value from an environment variable at startup, so you
    never commit the key itself. See <a href="/docs/guides/configuration/">Configuration</a>
    for the full three-layer cascade.
  </p>

  <h2>Onboarding</h2>
  <p>
    If cortex starts without a model configured, it prints an onboarding message explaining the
    three places a model can come from — it does not guess or default.
  </p>

  <div class="callout tip">
    <span class="ico">💡</span>
    <div class="callout-body">
      <strong>Tip:</strong> The transcript is committed to your terminal's own scrollback, not held
      in an alternate screen. A finished session stays scrollable and copyable after cortex exits.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="docs-pager"><Pager slug={slug} /></div>
</Doc>
